;; corpus/MANIFEST.edn — what is in corpus/, where it came from, under what licence.
;;
;; The rule this file exists to enforce: CC0, US public domain, or CC BY only.
;; Anything whose licence could not be *established* — by reading the publisher's
;; own statement, not by inferring one from the kind of institution — is not here.
;; The BIS central-bank policy-rate dataset (data.bis.org, WS_CBPOL) was the
;; natural first choice for the monthly table and was REJECTED on exactly that
;; rule; see :rejected at the foot of this file.
;;
;; Every table carries a coarse column of 2-12 distinct values, computed here at
;; fetch time, because `cat-col` (src/loci/content.clj) picks the *coarsest*
;; string column in that range and a raw `country` column (49-171 values) never
;; molds as Pivot or Bar. Exactly one table has a column literally named `month`,
;; because `timeseries?` keys on that name; the rest are annual and stay annual —
;; the gap between them is a finding about loci, not a defect in the data.
;;
;; :rows records source count -> committed count, and :filter the reduction, so a
;; reader can tell an extract from a sample and reproduce it.
;;
;; This file is plain EDN: every value is a literal, nothing here needs eval.

