   :rows    {:source 484956 :committed 352 :source-rows-examined 309710}
   :filter
   "A row qualifies if it has a non-blank Title (not \"untitled\" or \"unknown\"), a non-blank
Medium, and an Object Begin Date that parses as an integer in [-4000, 2030] and is not 0.
Qualifying rows are offered, in file order, to fourteen themed quotas, and the first N matches of
each are kept; an object is used at most once, by the first theme that claims it. Quotas:
  cobalt 45                    — Medium or Title contains \"cobalt\"
  dutch masters 55             — Artist Display Name matches one of 21 Dutch Golden Age names
                                 (rembrandt, vermeer, frans hals, ruisdael, jan steen, cuyp,
                                  claesz, hobbema, ter borch, de hooch, van goyen, gerard dou,
                                  gabriel metsu, avercamp, van heemskerck, maerten, jan van huysum,
                                  willem kalf, ambrosius bosschaert, adriaen van ostade,
                                  van de velde)
  dutch and netherlandish 30   — Culture contains \"dutch\" or \"netherlandish\", and an artist is named
  delft 25                     — Culture, Title or Medium contains \"delft\"
  chinese porcelain 45         — Culture contains \"china\" and Medium contains \"porcelain\"
  lead-bearing media 40        — Medium matches the word \"lead\", or \"lead-glaz\", \"white lead\",
                                 \"lead white\"
  breadth 14 per era bucket    — the row's era bucket, sampled at a stride of every 977th source
                                 row, so the corpus is not all seventeenth-century Holland
The scan stops once every quota is full, which happened at source row 309710 of 484956. Output is
sorted by (year, Title)."
   :columns {:passthrough ["Title" "Artist Display Name" "Culture" "Country" "Medium"]
             :computed    {"era"  "bucketed from Object Begin Date"
                           "year" "Object Begin Date, renamed"}
             :dropped     ["Department"]}
   :coarse-column "era"
   :coarse-values ["Before 500 CE" "500-1399" "1400-1599" "1600-1699"
                   "1700-1799" "1800-1899" "1900-1945" "After 1945"]
   :notes
   "MET's `Department` was fetched and then DROPPED: it has 10 distinct values in this extract, and
`cat-col` takes the coarsest 2-12-value string column, so Department would have quietly become the
Pivot axis instead of `era`.
`year` is a rename of `Object Begin Date`. Under the original header the column is neither
name-matched as a rate nor year-like (this extract spans -1900 to 2003), so `measure-col` would
treat it as a summable quantity and the Bar viewer would chart the SUM of object dates.
Titles and artist names keep MET's own `|` separator — between the Chinese and the English title,
and between co-authors. That is how the source writes them and it was left alone."
   :entangles ["cobalt" "china" "netherlands" "lead" "united states" "egypt" "iran"]}

